  "body": "## What changed\n\n- Plasma Profile takes a start pick and an exit pick. Its pick capability is `Ring` (`KindInfo::pick()`).\n- The picks are the operation-level `picks` of #3339 / PR #3871. This PR adds no field, no command and no MCP tool.\n- Start pick: the lead-in of the nearest closed contour lands on the projection of the pick on the profile. The pierce is at the start of that lead-in, in the scrap.\n- Exit pick: the torch cuts the full contour. Then it cuts on to the projection of the exit pick. The lead-out leaves there and the torch goes off at its end.\n- Small-hole rule: the pierce stays at the centre and there is no lead-out. A start pick sets where the straight lead-in meets the hole. An exit pick sets where the torch goes off. It must be at or past the overburn.\n- Each contour without a pick keeps its automatic seam.\n- A pick that a law cannot hold is refused by name. It is never moved. The text names the role and the point:\n  - a pick farther than 1.5 kerf widths from each closed profile;\n  - a pick when the operation has open runs only;\n  - a lead-in or a lead-out with no room beside the part at the pick (the pierce or the torch off would be on the part);\n  - a small-hole lead-in from the centre that would cross the part;\n  - a small-hole exit pick inside the overburn;\n  - an exit pick with control compensation (G41/G42), at the command door and in the generator.\n- The kerf law and the cover law still judge the complete path.\n- New generator door: `camcraft_motion::plasma::plasma_profile_picked`. `plasma_profile` calls it with no pick.\n\n## Cause\n\n`KindInfo::pick()` answered `NotTaken(PICK_OWED)` for Plasma Profile. The command refused each pick on the kind. The generator always chose the seam (`longest_mid`, or the point nearest the centre for a small hole).\n\n## Where the issue is silent (smallest change taken)\n\n- Which contour takes a pick: the closed contour whose profile is nearest. The reach is 1.5 kerf widths (the 2D contour uses 1.5 tool diameters).\n- How the cut gets to the exit: a run past the start in the cut direction. The stretch between the start and the exit is cut two times. A note on the path gives its length.\n- \"After the overburn\": only the small-hole rule has an overburn. There the exit must be at or past it. A contour with leads has no overburn, so the exit pick alone sets the run.\n- An exit pick with G41/G42 is refused by name. The programmed contour ends at its start, and a longer one needs a new proof of the compensation span. Mutation M2 showed that the generator emits a path without that refusal.\n- Waterjet: `WaterjetProfile` is on `main` now, with its own planner and tabs. This PR does not change it. A pick on it is still refused by name. The slice is #3983.\n- UI: this PR changes no UI file. The operation page reads `KindInfo::pick()`.\n\nThe decision record is `docs/decisions/3334-plasma-start-exit.md`.\n\n## Merge refresh and final validation\n\nFinal head: `1c5dce3386d3289800903f9181334a9c88869b55`.\nCurrent upstream main merged: `aef12fea67e0082e7ba835a3d9fcade8e2c11eb0`.\n\nClass: DELTA. The merge has three hand-resolved additive hunks:\n\n- `operation/pick_kinds.rs`: keep Plasma Profile `Ring` and `Thread | Drill | Bore` `HoleOrder` arms.\n- `tests/start_exit_shared.rs`: keep both `plasma` and `hole_order` modules.\n- `tests/start_exit_shared.rs`: keep both plasma and hole-order capability checks.\n\nWire exit refusal, Slot, turning and 5-axis contour entries stay present. Main's MCP tools and UI start/exit lists remain intact. Their diff against main is empty. No other code changed in this refresh.\n\nAll commands below ran on the final merge head, against the base above.\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` | 765 steps; 0 failed; 0 stalled; 7923 tests passed; 98 ignored |\n| `cargo clippy -j 16 -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings` | passed |\n| `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main` | 110 steps; 0 failed; 0 stalled; includes 109 reached targets and their release build |\n| app `start_exit_shared` | 28 passed: includes plasma, drilling hole order, turning and 5-axis contour |\n| app `slot_start_exit` | 10 passed |\n| app `wire_dxf_selection` | 14 passed: includes named arc exit refusal |\n| app `mcp_wire_contour` / `mcp_plasma` | 10 / 6 passed |\n| motion library | 706 passed; 22 ignored; includes all nine `plasma::picks_tests` |\n| app `golden_cl` | 34 passed |\n| app `example_catalog` | 43 passed; 4 ignored in debug; all 4 ignored cases passed in heavy |\n| app `example_catalog_adaptive` / `example_catalog_edge_work` | 1 / 1 passed |\n| UI library | 1684 passed; 8 ignored |\n\nPin proof on this merge: `every_kind_has_one_pick_capability_and_only_the_taken_ones_take_a_pick`.\n\n- Replace the plasma `Ring` arm with `NotTaken(PICK_OWED)`: RED, one assertion failure at `start_exit_shared.rs:79`. Restore: GREEN, one passed.\n- Replace the drilling `HoleOrder` arm with `NotTaken(PICK_OWED)`: RED, one assertion failure at `start_exit_shared.rs:81`. Restore: GREEN, one passed.\n\nEach mutation failed at its assertion. Neither failed at compilation. The source was restored after each run. The final worktree is clean. The shared suite registers both modules and runs all 28 tests.\n\nThe heavy plan excludes eight targets outside the diff reach. It also runs three quarantined tests. Each was red as expected, so the gate counted each step as passed. No unexpected test failed.\n\nThe earlier author run also mutation-checked reach, open-run, malformed-pick, small-hole, lead-refusal and control-compensation guards. The current refresh changes no such guard.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\n- The PR adds `crates/app/tests/golden/plasma_start_exit_picks.cl`. It records the picked plasma path.\n- This merge refresh changes no recorded program. No regeneration was needed for the additive conflict resolutions.\n- The final diff against main contains only that new `.cl` program. No existing `.nc`, `.cl`, or `examples/catalog/**` program changed.\n- `golden_cl` and all three debug catalog suites passed on the final head without regeneration.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The picked posted G-code on a physical machine. The CL golden pins the path. The plasma post suites passed locally.\n- The GUI. The PR changes no UI file relative to main, so before/after screenshots do not apply. The UI library suite passed.\n- A pick on many nested contours at nearly the same distance.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #3980, #3978, #3970, #3981: they touch `KindInfo::pick()` in `crates/app/src/operation/pick_kinds.rs` and the kind list in `crates/app/tests/start_exit_shared.rs`. Each changes the arm of its own kind. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #3981 also adds a submodule to the `start_exit_shared` suite (`mod turning;`). This PR adds `mod plasma;` at the same place.\n- #3832, #3674, #3103: they touch `crates/app/src/operation/types/sane.rs`, a different arm of the same `match`. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: Plasma Profile takes a start point and an exit point: the pierce is at the lead-in that lands on the start pick, the lead-out and the torch off are at the exit pick, and a pick that a plasma law cannot hold is refused by name.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3334\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
